WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
A cube-shaped tank sits in a garden.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:07.600
Each edge is one metre long, and
it's full to the brim with water.

3
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.950
Two friends say they'll carry
it across to the other side.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.220
A one-litre bottle of water has
a mass of about one kilogram.

5
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.720
So how heavy is the whole tank?

6
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.860
Ten kilograms?

7
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:19.880
A hundred?

8
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.300
Could two people really lift it?

9
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.500
In this mission, you'll see that
one metre is a hundred centimetres,

10
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.200
but a cubic metre is far more
than a hundred cubic centimetres.

11
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.600
You'll use the fact that one litre
is a thousand cubic centimetres.

12
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.020
And you'll work with density:
mass divided by volume.

13
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: decide whether
two people could lift the tank.
